      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we agree on adopting a map-like abstraction, then the key (currently attachmentId) should be taken out of BngAttachment and passed here as an input argument, exactly as in a map, where values are independent of the chosen key.\n\nThis would make the API straightforward (right now it doesn\u0027t look like a map API and one has to look at the BngAttachment interface to figure out where attachmentId comes from in the other methods). There are other benefits, such as unambiguous equality definition for BngAttachment which does not depend on the arbitrary key but on the attachment attributes only.",
